sam (docs): Quick note: spotted a C# quickstart example that both hardcodes an API key and blocks on async with .Result. This is a bad pattern for onboarding and can hang ASP.NET threadpools.

sam (docs): Example in docs: ```csharp
// BAD - hardcodes key and blocks
var client = new RedwoodClient("sk-abc123");
var out = client.GenerateAsync(req).Result;
Console.WriteLine(out.Text);
```

maya (devex): Ack. We should prefer FromEnvironment/DI and async/await everywhere. Also add a short note recommending not to put keys in repos and to use dotnet user-secrets for local dev. :memo:

igor (sdk): I'll prepare a PR to swap the snippet and update the README link targets. Proposed replacement: ```csharp
// GOOD - read from env + async/await
var client = RedwoodClient.FromEnvironment();
var response = await client.GenerateAsync(req).ConfigureAwait(false);
Console.WriteLine(response.Text);
```

igor (sdk): Adding an inline comment about token rotation and KMS for production. Will not show any literal keys in examples.

sam (docs): Please also update the quickstart index that the onboarding page references. The current gist used in the getting-started docs still has the old snippet.

docs-ci: link-checker: failure -> docs/quickstarts/csharp/README.md: line 37 contains suspicious token-like string. CI job: https://ci.internal/links/9802

maya (devex): Can we add a small docs-lint rule to detect literal sk- prefixes and synchronous Task.Result usage? Those are recurring issues.

igor (sdk): Good idea. I'll add a unit test to the docs validator that scans code fences for ".Result" and for regex /sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{6,}/. Will add to my PR.

sam (docs): Opening issue #912 and will link PR once ready. Also drafting a 1-paragraph changelog entry so customers who copied the gist get notified.

igor (sdk): PR 512 opened: replaces snippet, updates README, and amends the quickstart gist. https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/512

maya (devex): Once merged, I'll schedule a small explainer in the weekly digest to remind folks to rotate keys and prefer envs.

sam (docs): Thanks — tiny copy change but prevents a lot of onboarding headaches. If anyone finds similar snippets, drop them in #devex and tag me. :pray:
